# Force LF regardless of the checking-out platform's git config
# (core.autocrlf, safecrlf, etc). Everything under rootfs/ eventually runs
# inside the Linux container as a shebang script or gets fed straight to
# `node`/`sh` -- a CRLF checkout (Git's default behavior on many Windows
# setups) corrupts the shebang line (#!/bin/sh\r) and the container fails
# to start with a cryptic "No such file or directory" from tini, even
# though the file is right there. Seen in practice 2026-07-26: a local
# Windows `docker buildx build` from a fresh clone baked in CRLF
# entrypoint.sh and broke the running add-on on update.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

*.jpg binary
*.png binary
